  <!-- A full cloverleaf: I 84 (east-west, eastbound 290-293 at y -15, westbound 294-297 at y +15)
       crosses over I 205 (north-south, northbound 280-283 at x +15, southbound 284-287 at x -15)
       with no shared node. Each carriageway has four gores (20x, 21x, 22x, 23x at 300 m and 60 m
       either side of the crossing); eight motorway_link ramps join them, a loop (shape points
       31x-36x, radius 45 m) and an outer ramp (30x-37x) in each quadrant. Two-way frontage roads
       join each pair of carriageway ends, so the network is one.
       Expected: build 24 nodes, 32 segments, 36 edges; simplify removes none; stage A no clusters;
       twins: 20 candidates, 10 pairs (each run beside the opposite carriageway's run); stage B
       joins the eight ramp components (each connects I 84 with I 205) into one interchange
       replacing the 16 gores (44 members with the ramps' shape points), 20 internal edges (8
       ramps, 12 mainline runs between gores), all 4 x 4 (in, out) pairs allowed, U-turns through
       two loops included, 4 twin pairs carried (each approach with the opposite carriageway's
       departure on the same side): 9 nodes, 16 edges; connectivity keeps everything. -->
